{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"50e2ed04-edd2-4999-85cd-a384dba7a35d","status":"ERROR","response":"The `--print-timeout` flag is an option in the **Antigravity CLI (`agy`)** used when running prompts in non-interactive print/headless mode (`-p` / `--print`).\n\n---\n\n### Purpose \u0026 Behavior\n\n* **Function**: Defines the maximum duration the CLI will wait for the model/agent to complete its task and return the output before timing out.\n* **Default Value**: `5m` (5 minutes / `5m0s`).\n* **Format**: Standard Go/duration string format (e.g., `10m`, `15m`, `300s`, `1h`).\n\n---\n\n### Usage Examples\n\n#### 1. Basic Single Prompt with Extended Timeout\n```bash\nagy -p \"Review open PR changes and summarize risks\" --print-timeout 10m\n```\n\n#### 2. Complex Refactoring or Multi-step Tasks\n```bash\nagy --print \"Refactor codebase to support async database drivers\" --print-timeout 20m\n```\n\n#### 3. Automation \u0026 CI/CD Pipelines\n```bash\nagy -p \"Run test suite and fix failing unit tests\" --print-timeout 15m \u003e agent_output.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### When to Adjust It\n\n* **Increase the timeout** if long-running autonomous tasks (e.g., extensive research, full codebase scanning, running test suites) are getting cut off with a timeout error before completion.\n* **Decrease the timeout** in CI/CD environments where fast failure is preferred if an operation stalls.\n","error":"permission check failed for read_file \"/home/benchmark/.gemini/antigravity-cli\": Permission denied for read_file(/home/benchmark/.gemini/antigravity-cli). Matches hardcoded system protection boundary rule.","duration_seconds":24.064616292,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":66588,"output_tokens":1414,"thinking_tokens":761,"cache_read_tokens":32518,"total_tokens":68002}}}
